  "readTime": 1,
  "content": "<table align=\"center\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\">\n<tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<div>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr>\n<td align=\"left\" style=\"padding-left: 4px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"><p>#​497 — November 13, 2026</p></td>\n<td align=\"right\" style=\"padding-right: 4px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"><p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192928/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\">Read on the Web</a></p></td>\n</tr></table>\n<div style=\"color: #333;\">\n<div style=\"font-size: 2.7em; font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.3em; margin-bottom: 0px;\"> React Status</div>\n</div>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192893/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/jmcergdduhiy3e6s1glp.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192893/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.1em; line-height: 1.4em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"declarative-dragging.github.io\">Declarative Dragging</a></span> — Rather than designing drag and drop interactions as needed, what if you could <em>declare</em> the possible outcomes and let a library work out the interaction? <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192894/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\">Dragology</a> is an experimental React library for SVG interfaces that does just that. There are <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192895/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\">lots of demos</a> to try.</p>\n<p>Horowitz, Blinn, and Heer </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192892/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\"><img height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/c_limit,w_480,h_480,q_auto/copm/baddea09.png\" style=\"padding-top: 12px; padding-left: 12px; line-height: 100%;\" width=\"160\"/></a>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192892/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"sentry.io\">Debug Errors and Agents Faster: Sentry Changelog Live</a></span> — A walkthrough of what’s new for debugging errors and performance issues, including fixing production bugs with Seer and tracing the agents you build. Live Q&amp;A. Nov 18, 10am PT. <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192892/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\">Save your spot</a>.</p>\n<p>Sentry <span style=\"margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px;\">sponsor</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><span>📊</span> <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192896/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"e18e.dev\">e18e's Ongoing Benchmarks for JavaScript Meta-Frameworks</a></span> — e18e is now benchmarking meta-frameworks like Next.js, Nuxt, and Astro on everything from install and build costs to SSR throughput, alongside Core Web Vitals data. Built with input from maintainers, <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192897/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\">the results</a> can be tracked release by release and have already led to fixes in Nuxt, React, and Solid.</p>\n<p>e18e Project </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><strong>IN BRIEF:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>⚠️ Using Vite? <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192898/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">A critical flaw</a> allows remote code execution on dev servers exposed to the network with <code>--host</code> or <code>server.host</code>. Update to 8.3.7, 8.2.5, 8.1.7, 7.3.8 or 6.4.6.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192899/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Storybook 11 beta now has an official post</a>. React projects get faster, more accurate component metadata, and there are type-safe stories and official skills for agents. The final release is due in December.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>React's <code>&lt;form&gt;</code> docs now explain <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192900/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">how to keep field values after an Action</a>, and <code>requestFormReset</code> gets <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192901/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">a reference page</a> of its own.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192902/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"ui-sdk.dev\">UI SDK: Vercel and shadcn's Headless UI Behaviors Library</a></span> — A low-level library of behaviors, like keyboard navigation, popups, drag and drop, that you compose into your own components. A core idea is to give a solid base for agents to build full components from. In beta, but you can <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192903/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\">get started now</a>.</p>\n<p>shadcn (Vercel) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192904/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"blog.x.com\">How X is Rebuilding Its Web App with React, Relay and Vite</a></span> — X/Twitter is replacing its decade-old client-rendered React app with a stack built around streaming SSR and Suspense. Lab tests show profiles displaying posts much sooner, and the hydration and chunking fixes make this an interesting case study.</p>\n<p>Yagiz Nizipli (X) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>📊 <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192906/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Six React Chart Libraries vs Hand-Written SVG</a> – The results are close at native speed but with large gaps under CPU throttling or with large datasets. <cite>Pavel Gusev</cite></p>\n<p>📊 <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192905/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Remix v3 vs TanStack Start: Fast Pages, Thin Ecosystem</a> – Comparing the same site built in React-free Remix v3 and TanStack Start. <cite>Jonathan Arnault (Marmelab)</cite></p>\n<p>📱 <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192907/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">How Five Web Developers Built an iOS Keyboard Extension with Expo</a> <cite>Anirudh Coontoor (Supernova)</cite></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0;\"><p>🛠  Code, Tools &amp; Libraries</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192908/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/rzyk9hdnriuqphjxnsvj.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192908/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"textjs.org\">Text.js: React Apps That Render in the DevTools Console</a></span> — Continuing the trend of rendering React apps <em>everywhere</em>, this new framework heads to DevTools as a host environment, supporting App Router-style routing, Suspense, keyboard input and ASCII fonts. Open the console on the page to see it in action!</p>\n<p>Anomaly </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192909/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"ccheever.expo.app\">Exact: A New Rust-Powered App Framework from Expo's Co-Founder</a></span> — It <em>isn't</em> React as the UI is written in a small, constrained language called Contract that's designed specifically for agents to write and test, but <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192910/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\">𝕏 Andrew Clark says</a> it's <em>\"eerily similar\"</em> to what he thinks React 20 is shaping up to be.</p>\n<p>Charlie Cheever </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192929/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"github.com\">React Shepherd 8.0: Guided Tours for Apps, Now with a Leaner Engine</a></span> — The React wrapper  (<a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192930/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\">React docs here</a>) for <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192912/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\">Shepherd</a>, a popular library for building step-based on-page tours. <em>Note that it's AGPL, with a paid license for commercial use.</em></p>\n<p>Ship Shape </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192913/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">EmbedPDF 3.0</a> – Powerful PDF viewer with a drop-in React component and a headless library for adding your own UI. (<a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192914/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Demo</a>.)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192915/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">react-virtualized 10.0</a> – The original list and grid virtualization library, modernized. Now in TypeScript, built on function components, and requires React 18+.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>📱 <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192916/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">React Native Audio API 1.0</a> – Software Mansion's Web Audio API for React Native goes stable. Adds spatial audio, and FFmpeg is now opt-in.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192917/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Mantine 9.8</a> – Adds an emoji picker package, plus new <code>Diff</code>, <code>PhoneInput</code> and week and quarter picker components.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192919/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">BagUI</a> – A <code>shadcn/ui</code> registry of blocks and templates for SaaS landing pages, like pricing and hero sections.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px;\">\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>📰 Classifieds</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>🔍 Can ChatGPT and Claude read your React site? Run a free SEO and GEO scan with <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192920/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Fimo</a> and see what they miss. By the Strapi team.</p>\n<p>🎬 Stop approving mobile PRs nobody ran. An agent tests each one on <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192921/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Expo Simulators</a> and puts the recording in the PR.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192922/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Build durable AI agents &amp; workflows in TypeScript with Trigger.dev</a>. If steps fail or code deploys, tasks pick up right where they left off.</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0;\"><p>📢  Elsewhere in the ecosystem</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192923/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/wjp1pnhalfiz0jddculv.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192923/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Vectoys</a> is a set of React components that render phones, laptops and other small 3D objects as SVG, with interactive HTML inside their screens. Could be handy for mockups or 'in-situ' teasers on your homepage.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>🤖 Chrome's <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192924/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Modern Web Guidance 1.0</a> is a set of skills that steer coding agents toward modern, Baseline-aware HTML and CSS. The team has also listed <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192925/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">the 'top 10 things AI gets wrong'</a> when building for the Web.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Need a clip of a component or animation for a PR or README? Paul Irish's <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192926/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">chrome-capture</a> tool can record a Chrome tab to an MP4 at 60fps with a single <code>npx</code> command.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>📊 The <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192927/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">State of JavaScript 2026 survey</a> is now open if you want to get involved.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n</div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n",
  "attachments": []
}